Mouse brain and cerebrovasculature, photon-counting micro-CT, DICOM slices in this folder

Attribution:
  Data by Huang Siyi / Han Xin / Li Zuoyan / Zhou Enze / Wang Shaoyang / Liu Qian / Xie Tianwu
  "A multi-material photon-counting micro-CT dataset of mouse brain with voxel-wise cerebrovascular annotations", Zenodo record 22092756
  https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22092756

License:
  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Changes made to the original data:
  - cropped to the head and converted from NIfTI to DICOM; resampled along the slice axis from 670 to 512 slices (spacing 0.02292 mm -> 0.02999 mm)
  - the bundled vessel mask is registered as the contrast segment, and the intracranial support region minus the vessels as the soft-tissue (brain) segment
  - 3D reconstruction and rendering in this application
  - stored values are photon-counting CT processed values, not calibrated Hounsfield units

Terms in short (the license text at the link above is the only binding text):
  - You may use and adapt the data, commercially or not, if you give appropriate credit.
  - This license applies to the data in this folder only, not to the rest of this application.

